<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">A&nbsp;few&nbsp;things.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2949 is a phenomenon affecting approximately 3% of all analogue television sets ever produced</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That is <em>a lot</em> of televisions. Also how was that figure determined?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>appearance of non-humanoid faces</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Can faces really even be non-humanoid? Doesn't anything face-like enough to be called a face already sort of look like a person?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>vague movements in the background noise</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Static already is a sort of vague movement, right?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Continuous observation of the phenomena</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I <em>think</em> this should be the singular &quot;phenomenon&quot;, unless I'm reading incorrectly.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Such surfaces through which SCP-2949-1 instances have been seen disappearing into include mirrors, windows, and other television screens.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure you really need to give examples of reflective surfaces.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
